                        <provenance type="#rejected"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_474">St Albans,
                            Hertfordshire, Benedictine abbey of St Alban</orgName> <p>This
                            attribution was accepted (albeit with a query) in the second edition of
                            Medieval Libraries of Great Britain (1964). However, the attribution was
                            later rejected in the Supplement (1987). The corresponding Medieval
                            Libraries of Great Britain index originally gave the following evidence
                            (in Ker's handwriting): 'St Albans decoration and script. The remaining
                            large initial - 14 others have been cut out - is by the artist of the
                            Hildesheim manuscript.' However, the index card also has a later note in
                            Andrew Watson's handwriting, explaining why the attribution was
                            subsequently rejected: 'R M. Thomson, <title>Manuscripts from St. Albans
                            Abbey</title> (1982), i, 124 lists as a MS whose artists are associable
                            with St. Albans but not as one owned by the abbey
                            itself.'</p></provenance>
